WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:01.620
Instructor: The final thing I'll show you here

00:01.620 --> 00:04.380
with interactive Rebase is how we can completely

00:04.380 --> 00:06.690
remove a commit, not just the message

00:06.690 --> 00:09.187
but the entire commit and its changes.

00:09.187 --> 00:11.880
So I have this one horrible commit I made.

00:11.880 --> 00:12.900
Let's say it was an accident.

00:12.900 --> 00:15.240
It's silly, but in all reality

00:15.240 --> 00:16.350
there might be work you've done

00:16.350 --> 00:19.800
on a branch that you just don't want anymore, especially

00:19.800 --> 00:22.012
as you're about to share this branch with other people.

00:22.012 --> 00:24.810
So I faked that by de making a commit

00:24.810 --> 00:28.350
claiming it was from my cat, my JavaScript app.js

00:28.350 --> 00:30.600
file has a bunch of random nonsense, and then

00:30.600 --> 00:33.840
a commit message that says, my cat made this commit.

00:33.840 --> 00:35.550
So I wanna get rid of that.

00:35.550 --> 00:37.650
I'll just show you right now.

00:37.650 --> 00:40.650
If I take a look at the app.js file

00:40.650 --> 00:43.200
using the aptly named cat command

00:43.200 --> 00:44.700
this is what's in there, right?

00:44.700 --> 00:45.660
I can see this here.

00:45.660 --> 00:48.660
If I open it, I wanna get rid of that.

00:48.660 --> 00:50.340
I mean, I could delete it of course, but then

00:50.340 --> 00:52.740
I have to make a commit that says something like, you know

00:52.740 --> 00:54.660
deleting work for my cat.

00:54.660 --> 00:56.940
I just wanna drop that commit entirely.

00:56.940 --> 00:59.613
So I need to figure out how far back to go.

01:00.870 --> 01:02.640
It's just two commits to go.

01:02.640 --> 01:04.020
So that's, I could just do that.

01:04.020 --> 01:04.853
Go back two.

01:04.853 --> 01:06.960
So interactive rebase two.

01:06.960 --> 01:08.280
So I'm gonna do that.

01:08.280 --> 01:13.280
Git rebase dash I again, just rebasing in place.

01:13.500 --> 01:17.730
So head tilde two, it opens it up.

01:17.730 --> 01:22.730
Here's that commit, and instead of pick or reword or fix up

01:23.100 --> 01:27.270
I'm going to drop, which will remove the commit entirely.

01:27.270 --> 01:28.290
All righty.

01:28.290 --> 01:30.330
So we're gonna go ahead and try that.

01:30.330 --> 01:32.760
I don't know why I just went to my terminal.

01:32.760 --> 01:36.180
I'm gonna do drop that commit

01:36.180 --> 01:40.080
and then X out of here, I saved.

01:40.080 --> 01:45.080
And now first of all, if I type git log, that commit is not

01:45.570 --> 01:46.440
showing up, right?

01:46.440 --> 01:50.040
I don't see the message, but also the changes are gone.

01:50.040 --> 01:52.620
If I go to my editor, that file is still here

01:52.620 --> 01:54.810
because I created it in a different commit

01:54.810 --> 01:57.330
but the contents are gone.

01:57.330 --> 02:00.900
So now I have a completely rewritten history on this branch

02:00.900 --> 02:04.240
my feature branch, and we could compare it.

02:04.240 --> 02:06.570
So if we just take a look here, right?

02:06.570 --> 02:09.870
We only have one, two, three, four, five, six total commits.

02:09.870 --> 02:12.900
And they're all, I guess in present tense

02:12.900 --> 02:17.670
although you know it, maybe I want to uppercase all of them.

02:17.670 --> 02:21.780
So here we have an uppercase C, or the other option

02:21.780 --> 02:23.490
would be to make this lowercase.

02:23.490 --> 02:24.720
So we could do that, right?

02:24.720 --> 02:27.210
We know how to do that actually, if it's the most

02:27.210 --> 02:30.330
recent commit, the easiest way is to use git

02:30.330 --> 02:34.260
commit dash amend, which I showed you quite a long time ago.

02:34.260 --> 02:38.010
You may not remember, but if I do this, it opens

02:38.010 --> 02:40.050
up the most recent commit and it allows me

02:40.050 --> 02:41.610
to edit the commit message.

02:41.610 --> 02:45.630
But also I could add stuff in if I did a git add first

02:45.630 --> 02:47.100
and then commit amend.

02:47.100 --> 02:48.950
So I'm gonna close outta this though.

02:50.130 --> 02:53.970
And now if I do my git log, everything's all lowercase.

02:53.970 --> 02:56.100
I don't know, may just keep it consistent, right?

02:56.100 --> 02:57.300
It's just another way of editing

02:57.300 --> 03:00.360
commits of rewriting history.

03:00.360 --> 03:03.180
Okay, so we'll switch back to master from here.

03:03.180 --> 03:07.563
Git switch master and do a, oh no, it's main, isn't it?

03:09.240 --> 03:11.700
And then I'll do a git log one line.

03:11.700 --> 03:13.260
Way more commits.

03:13.260 --> 03:17.070
As you can see, very inconsistent tense.

03:17.070 --> 03:18.480
We collapse some of these down.

03:18.480 --> 03:20.130
We mushed them together.

03:20.130 --> 03:22.170
This one here with that one.

03:22.170 --> 03:24.150
And then these three, we combined

03:24.150 --> 03:26.973
we dropped this one, we rewrote history.
